      <div class="col-11">
	<div class="row">
	  <div class="col-sm-2">
            <h2 class="section-heading mb-0 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
              <span class="section-heading-upper tw">Foundations</span>
            </h2>
	  </div>
	  <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
	  <div class="col-sm-8 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
            <p class="mb-0">When we consider what makes up a person, we think about many things - their body, their personality, their experiences, their knowledge, their likes and dislikes, even what they do. Within Yomonsni, we think of this in three overlapping layers: self, mind, and body. </p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0">Mind, self and body all work together. Your emotional well being, or stress levels can impact your health, and your health impacts your thoughts, etc. So as you work on developing as a person, it is important to work on all layers in a harmonious approach, growing all of you rather than allowing yourself to unbalance. </p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
	  </div>
	</div inner-row>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	
	<div class="row p-2 tw">
	  <div class="col-sm-2">
            <h2 class="section-heading mb-0 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
              <span class="section-heading-upper tw">Mind</span>
            </h2>
	  </div>
	  <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
	  <div class="col-sm-8 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
            <p class="mb-0">Your mind is made up of your knowledge, experience, analysis, attention and focus. Here is where you solve problems, ponder the nature of the universe, work logically and perform rational judgements.</p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
	  </div>
	</div innerrow>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	
	
	<div class="row">
	  <div class="col-sm-2">
            <h2 class="section-heading mb-0 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
              <span class="section-heading-upper tw">Body</span>
            </h2>
	  </div>
	  <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
	  <div class="col-sm-8 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
            <p class="mb-0">Your body is the raw physicality of your existence. Skin, muscles, organs, skeleton. Your body is also quite a bit of non-human material - bacteria, viruses and sometimes parasites that dwell within you symboiotically.</p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
	  </div>
	</div innerrow>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	
	
	<div class="row">
	  <div class="col-sm-2">
            <h2 class="section-heading mb-0 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
              <span class="section-heading-upper tw">Self</span>
            </h2>
	  </div>
	  <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
	  <div class="col-sm-8 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
            <p class="mb-0">Self is perhaps your emotional center. This is your sense of intuition, connection, creativity. When you feel, this is where that resides.</p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
